---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { SITE } from '../lib/site'
const updated = '31 May 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — The Reel Vault"
  description="The terms governing your use of The Reel Vault, including third-party content, disclaimers and takedown requests."
>
  <div class="section-head">
    <div><span class="kicker">The fine print</span><h2>Terms of Use</h2></div>
  </div>
  <p class="type" style="margin-top:-6px">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <article class="prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <p>
      By using {SITE.name} (the "Site") you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please
      do not use the Site.
    </p>

    <h3>The service</h3>
    <p>
      The Reel Vault is a free, curated guide to public-domain and freely-available film. We
      organise and provide commentary on material that is hosted and streamed by third
      parties — principally the Internet Archive. We do not host the films ourselves, and we
      provide the Site on an "as is" and "as available" basis.
    </p>

    <h3>Third-party content</h3>
    <p>
      Films, video, images and much of the descriptive text are supplied by third parties,
      including the Internet Archive and Wikipedia. We do not own this material and make no
      representation about its accuracy, completeness or copyright status beyond the metadata
      those sources provide. Your use of third-party content may also be subject to the terms
      of the service that hosts it.
    </p>

    <h3>Copyright and takedown requests</h3>
    <p>
      We aim to feature only works that are in the public domain or otherwise free to view.
      If you are a rights holder and believe a work has been linked or described here in a way
      that infringes your rights, please contact us at
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> with: (1) identification
      of the work, (2) the URL on this Site, (3) your contact details, and (4) a statement of
      your good-faith belief and authority to act. Because the underlying file is hosted by a
      third party, you may also wish to contact that host directly. We will respond to valid
      requests promptly, including by removing links where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h3>Acceptable use</h3>
    <p>
      You agree not to misuse the Site: no attempting to disrupt it, no automated scraping
      that places an unreasonable load on it or on the third-party services it links to, and
      no use that violates applicable law.
    </p>

    <h3>Disclaimer of warranties</h3>
    <p>
      The Site is provided without warranties of any kind, express or implied. We do not
      guarantee that any particular film will be available, that information will be accurate,
      or that the Site will be uninterrupted or error-free. Availability of any title depends
      entirely on the third party that hosts it.
    </p>

    <h3>Limitation of liability</h3>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} will not be liable for any indirect,
      incidental or consequential damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, the
      Site or any third-party content reached through it.
    </p>

    <h3>Changes</h3>
    <p>
      We may revise these terms from time to time. Continued use of the Site after changes
      take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:24px">
      Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
